WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.505
Mr. Gwarg stared at his watch as he waited for the monsters to calm down.

2
00:00:08.506 --> 00:00:11.966
"We're losing precious time," he said.

3
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:17.841
When everyone had finally grown quiet again, Mr. Gwarg grabbed his clipboard.

4
00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:21.760
"Let’s review our Field Day rules."

5
00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:24.317
"Ugh." Mog groaned.

6
00:00:24.318 --> 00:00:27.378
"We've heard these rules twenty times already!

7
00:00:27.379 --> 00:00:29.735
Can't we just get started?"

8
00:00:29.736 --> 00:00:33.377
"That's enough, Mog!" Mr. Freaky snapped.

9
00:00:33.378 --> 00:00:35.187
"The rules are important.

10
00:00:35.188 --> 00:00:38.962
That's how everything stays under control around here."

11
00:00:38.963 --> 00:00:44.486
He took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

12
00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:50.705
"Okay, first rule—no magic spells," Mr. Gwarg announced.

13
00:00:50.706 --> 00:00:55.679
"Aww!" Several witches and wizards started complaining.

14
00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.030
"What about hexes?" somebody asked. "Can we use those?"

15
00:01:00.031 --> 00:01:05.356
"No!" Mr. Gwarg snapped. "No magic whatsoever!"

16
00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:07.616
A vampire raised her hand.

17
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:14.710
"Can I turn into a bat and fly around?"

18
00:01:14.711 --> 00:01:16.860
Mr. Gwarg blinked at her.

19
00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:20.751
"You're not even on a team, Vanessa," he said.

20
00:01:20.752 --> 00:01:25.215
"But if you were on a team, yes, you could do that.

21
00:01:25.216 --> 00:01:28.275
That's not magic—it's an ability."

22
00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:36.508
"So it's okay if I make my feet bigger to run faster?" Carly asked.

23
00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:39.123
The gym teacher scratched his head.

24
00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:43.983
"I guess so. But I don't think it would actually improve your speed."

25
00:01:43.984 --> 00:01:48.018
Monsters kept raising their hands to ask more questions. Finally

26
00:01:48.019 --> 00:01:53.169
Mr. Gwarg lifted his whistle and gave a long, loud blast. "I

27
00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.528
don't have time to answer all these questions. Look,

28
00:01:58.529 --> 00:02:01.355
there's really only one rule. And

29
00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:05.423
that's this one—just play fair. Now

30
00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:10.607
Team Orange and Team Black, line up for our first event. It's

31
00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:13.613
the tug-of-war!" "Phew,"

32
00:02:13.614 --> 00:02:19.297
Ben murmured to Pixel. "That took forever." The

33
00:02:19.298 --> 00:02:27.099
spectators cheered as the two teams took their places in the center of the field. Ben

34
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:33.375
could see that a long rope had been laid over a shallow pit filled with mud. The

35
00:02:33.376 --> 00:02:38.195
teams lined up on opposite sides of the pit. Then

36
00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:41.607
each player gripped the rope. Suddenly

37
00:02:41.608 --> 00:02:46.251
Ben spotted the sixth member of Team Orange. "Oh,

38
00:02:46.252 --> 00:02:49.767
no!" he gasped. Last

39
00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:53.992
in line on the opposite side of the rope was Gaby. And

40
00:02:53.993 --> 00:02:57.516
Gaby was strong—really strong! She

41
00:02:57.517 --> 00:03:01.475
must be what Zork meant by his "secret weapon." Waldo

42
00:03:01.476 --> 00:03:05.960
had spotted her too. "Not good," he muttered. "Gaby

43
00:03:05.961 --> 00:03:09.033
is even stronger when she's mad." Ben

44
00:03:09.034 --> 00:03:13.778
gulped. "And is she mad about something right now?" Waldo

45
00:03:13.779 --> 00:03:17.780
nodded. "She's really mad at me. She

46
00:03:17.781 --> 00:03:21.875
said that I should have made Mog choose her for Team Black." Ben

47
00:03:21.876 --> 00:03:25.372
drew in a breath. "Well,

48
00:03:25.373 --> 00:03:28.965
there's no time to worry about that now," he said. "We're

49
00:03:28.966 --> 00:03:31.116
about to start." "Okay,

50
00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:37.326
guys." Mog turned around to talk to his team from his spot as first in line. "Here's

51
00:03:37.327 --> 00:03:43.608
the plan. As soon as the game starts, pull the rope as fast and as hard as you can. Maybe

52
00:03:43.609 --> 00:03:46.450
we can take Team Orange by surprise." "Got

53
00:03:46.451 --> 00:03:50.795
it!" everybody said, gripping the rope tightly. Mr.

54
00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.309
Gwarg lifted his whistle. "The

55
00:03:53.429 --> 00:03:58.598
first team to pull the other team into the mud wins," he announced. "Is

56
00:03:58.599 --> 00:04:00.727
everybody ready?" Both

57
00:04:00.728 --> 00:04:06.331
team captains nodded, and then— tweet! The whistle blew to start the game.

58
00:04:06.332 --> 00:04:10.370
"Pull, Black!" Mog shouted. "Pull hard!"

59
00:04:10.371 --> 00:04:14.412
Ben and the others tugged as fast and as hard as they could.

60
00:04:14.413 --> 00:04:18.147
To Ben's surprise, Mog's plan worked perfectly.

61
00:04:18.148 --> 00:04:25.469
In an instant Zork and his team were flying across the ground, and Zork was teetering on the edge of the mud pit.

62
00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:36.021
"Pull!" Mog screamed. "Harder!"

63
00:04:36.022 --> 00:04:41.436
"Yes!" Ben thought. "Zork's going to fall in! We're going to win!"

64
00:04:41.437 --> 00:04:45.641
Then, with a loud ka-snap! , the rope

65
00:04:45.642 --> 00:04:50.367
broke. Both teams tumbled backward, landing hard on the ground.

66
00:04:50.368 --> 00:04:56.530
"Time out!" Mr. Gwarg rushed forward to look at the broken rope.

67
00:04:56.531 --> 00:05:00.813
"What in the world happened? I buy the best ropes in Monsterville.

68
00:05:00.814 --> 00:05:03.793
I've never seen one break before."

69
00:05:03.794 --> 00:05:07.193
Waldo went to take a look.

70
00:05:07.194 --> 00:05:10.738
"I can fix that, Mr. Gwarg. I know a good spell."

71
00:05:10.739 --> 00:05:13.637
"Me too!" Brunhilda called.

72
00:05:13.638 --> 00:05:17.754
"Monsters!" Mr. Freaky was flapping his arms.

73
00:05:17.755 --> 00:05:22.910
"What did Mr. Gwarg tell you—no magic during Field Day events!"

74
00:05:22.911 --> 00:05:25.256
"Sorry!" Waldo called.

75
00:05:25.257 --> 00:05:28.192
"We forgot," Brunhilda added.

76
00:05:28.193 --> 00:05:32.868
Mr. Gwarg ran to an equipment shed to get another rope.

77
00:05:32.869 --> 00:05:36.434
Then he told the two teams to line up again.

78
00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:39.546
"Okay, everyone, take your places."

79
00:05:39.547 --> 00:05:44.861
The teams gathered on their sides of the pit once more.

80
00:05:44.862 --> 00:05:50.826
"Go!" Mr. Gwarg shouted, and both teams began pulling with all their might again.

81
00:05:50.827 --> 00:05:57.988
This time, though, Team Orange wasn't surprised by Team Black's strategy; they were ready for it.

82
00:05:57.989 --> 00:06:05.417
Back and forth the rope tugged for several minutes, with neither team making much progress.

83
00:06:05.418 --> 00:06:12.466
The spectators on the field were cheering loudly as the cheerleaders did cartwheels across the field.

84
00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:16.135
"Go, Orange! Go, Black!"

85
00:06:16.136 --> 00:06:22.300
Then all at once, the air went deadly silent.

